import lib/cadkernel/brep_geometry.dl

function geometry extra check {boolean:condition}:
    execute:
        if condition = false:
            print "B-rep geometry extra assertion failed" as a line
            @intrinsic("call", "libc", "exit", nothing, 1)

function the geometry extra point {a number:x} {a number:y} {a number:z}:
    execute:
        return a cad vector3 with x x, y y and z z

set sphere to the cad surface of (a cad sphere with frame the cad xy plane and radius 2.0)
set hits to the cad ray hits of sphere from (the geometry extra point 5.0 0.0 0.0) along (the geometry extra point -1.0 0.0 0.0)
geometry extra check hits's valid
geometry extra check ((the length of hits's values) = 2)
geometry extra check ((the item at 0 in hits's values) = 3.0)
geometry extra check ((the item at 1 in hits's values) = 7.0)
set retained to hits
set hits to the cad ray hits of sphere from the cad zero vector3 along the cad x axis
geometry extra check ((the item at 0 in hits's values) = -2.0)
geometry extra check ((the item at 1 in hits's values) = 2.0)
geometry extra check ((the item at 0 in retained's values) = 3.0)
set infinity to (1.0 as a 64 bit floating-point number) / 0.0
set hits to the cad ray hits of sphere from (the geometry extra point infinity 0.0 0.0) along the cad zero vector3
geometry extra check hits's valid
geometry extra check ((the length of hits's values) = 1)
set nonfinite to the item at 0 in hits's values
geometry extra check (nonfinite != nonfinite)
set tangents to the cad tangents of sphere at parameters 0.0 and 0.0
geometry extra check tangents's valid
geometry extra check (tangents's u's y = 2.0)
geometry extra check (tangents's v's z = 2.0)
set normal to the cad normal of sphere at parameters 0.0 and 0.0
geometry extra check normal's valid
geometry extra check (normal's value's x = 1.0)
set inverse to the cad parameters on sphere nearest (the geometry extra point 0.0 0.0 2.0)
geometry extra check (inverse's valid = false)

set cylinder to the cad surface of (a cad cylinder with base the cad xy plane and radius 3.0)
set tangents to the cad tangents of cylinder at parameters 0.0 and 4.0
geometry extra check (tangents's u's y = 3.0)
geometry extra check (tangents's v's z = 1.0)
set inverse to the cad parameters on cylinder nearest (the geometry extra point 3.0 0.0 4.0)
geometry extra check inverse's valid
geometry extra check (inverse's value's x = 0.0)
geometry extra check (inverse's value's y = 4.0)
set framed to the cad frame of cylinder
geometry extra check framed's valid

set plane to the cad surface of the cad xy plane
set hits to the cad ray hits of plane from (the geometry extra point 0.0 0.0 2.0) along (the geometry extra point 0.0 0.0 -1.0)
geometry extra check ((the item at 0 in hits's values) = 2.0)
set hits to the cad ray hits of plane from the cad zero vector3 along the cad x axis
geometry extra check hits's valid
geometry extra check ((the length of hits's values) = 0)
set torus to the cad surface of (a cad torus with frame the cad xy plane, major radius 2.0 and minor radius 3.0)
set hits to the cad ray hits of torus from the cad zero vector3 along the cad x axis
geometry extra check (hits's valid = false)
set point to the cad point on torus at parameters 0.2 and 3.141592653589793
set inverse to the cad parameters on torus nearest point
geometry extra check inverse's valid
geometry extra check ((the cad distance from point to (the cad point on torus at parameters inverse's value's x and inverse's value's y)) < 1e-12)

set clone to the cad clone of torus
geometry extra check (clone = torus)
set clone's torus's majorRadius to 8.0
geometry extra check ((clone = torus) = false)
geometry extra check (torus's nurbs's owner = (0 as a pointer to an integer))
print "B-rep geometry extra checks passed" as a line
